Regional Market Dynamics
Middle East: Dominates premium catering with Dubai International Airport handling over 95,000 premium meals daily. Local halal certification requirements create barriers for international caterers.
Asia-Pacific: Fastest-growing region at 6.9% CAGR, driven by Chinese domestic traffic recovery and Indian LCC expansion. Japanese caterers lead in precision and presentation standards.
Europe: Tight environmental regulations push sustainable packaging adoption, with 73% of meals now served in compostable containers.
North America: Hub-and-spoke networks favor large-scale centralized kitchens, though labor disputes have caused service disruptions at major hubs.

